## Key Lesson

An image rebuild doesn't need to touch application code to break production — any unpinned dependency in a Dockerfile is a live landmine that can detonate on the *next unrelated* CI trigger, with an arbitrary delay between "build" and "blast" (4 days build-to-blast here, extended by the prod server being powered off in between). Floating version references — whether `pip install kubernetes` with no version or `curl .../stable.txt` for kubectl — should be treated as the same category of risk and pinned consistently, not just the one that happened to bite first.